//RS 
//RS /// D-SWIZZLE1 (ratified 2026-06-27): named lane swizzles on vector/SIMD types.
//RS /// Members `x`/`y`/`z`/`w` name lanes 0..3; patterns like `v.xyz`, `v.yx`, and
//RS /// write-swizzles `v.xy = Vec2(…)` are blessed field access on `Vec2`/`Vec3`/`Vec4`
//RS /// and `F32x4`/`F64x2` only (matrices are not swizzleable). Overlapping write
//RS /// patterns (`v.xx = …`) are diagnosed (E3111); out-of-range lanes (E3110).
//RS 
//RS /// D-LINALG1 (ratified 2026-06-24): the built-in linear-algebra value types.
//RS /// Vectors `Vec2`/`Vec3`/`Vec4` and square matrices `Mat3`/`Mat4` (column-major,
//RS /// `F64` components). Methods `.dot()`/`.cross()` (Vec3 only)/`.matmul()`, plus
//RS /// `.length()`/`.normalize()`; element-wise `+`/`-`, scalar `*`, and `Mat * Vec`.
//RS /// A closed compiler-provided family — the user-facing aliases over the generic
//RS /// `Vec<N>`/`Matrix<M,N>` substrate. Plain std math (no `unsafe`).
//RS pub const LINALG_VEC2_TYPE: &str = "Vec2";
//RS pub const LINALG_VEC3_TYPE: &str = "Vec3";
//RS pub const LINALG_VEC4_TYPE: &str = "Vec4";
//RS pub const LINALG_MAT3_TYPE: &str = "Mat3";
//RS pub const LINALG_MAT4_TYPE: &str = "Mat4";
//RS 
//RS /// D-LAYOUT1 / D-LAYOUT-GATES1 (ratified 2026-06-28/29) + D-LAYOUT-CTOR1
//RS /// (D-VERDICT-1306-1, ratified 2026-07-28): the built-in constraint-layout
//RS /// value types. `HVar`/`VVar` are axis-typed layout variables
//RS /// (horizontal/vertical); `LengthVar` is an axis-neutral scalar length that
//RS /// combines with either axis. GATE 1: comparison operators (`>=`/`<=`/`==`)
//RS /// on these types produce a `Constraint`, not `Bool` — a closed-operator
//RS /// blessing on this family only (same category as D-SIMD2). GATE 2: all five
//RS /// names enter the compiler's closed type family (`core_type_known`). A
//RS /// closed compiler-provided family — no user `+`/comparison overload.
//RS /// Cross-axis combination (`HVar` with `VVar`) is E-LAYOUT-AXIS-MISMATCH
//RS /// (E2932). `Layout` is the solver/container value constructed by
//RS /// `name :: Layout{ … }` (D-DOTCTOR3 element body of `Constraint`s);
//RS /// `Constraint` is a registered, prioritizable constraint handle
//RS /// (`.required()`/`.strong()`/`.medium()`/`.weak()`). Method API
//RS /// (`Layout.h`/`v`/`value`/`suggest`/`add`, `Constraint.gte`/…) is the
//RS /// desugar underlayment. The retired user spelling `LayoutHandle` is E2936.
//RS pub const LAYOUT_HVAR_TYPE: &str = "HVar";
//RS pub const LAYOUT_VVAR_TYPE: &str = "VVar";
//RS pub const LAYOUT_LENGTHVAR_TYPE: &str = "LengthVar";
//RS pub const LAYOUT_CONSTRAINT_TYPE: &str = "Constraint";
//RS pub const LAYOUT_TYPE: &str = "Layout";
//RS /// Retired D-LAYOUT1 spelling of `Layout` — teaching error E2936 only.
//RS pub const LAYOUT_HANDLE_TYPE_RETIRED: &str = "LayoutHandle";
//RS /// Transitional alias — every consumer should migrate to `LAYOUT_TYPE`.
//RS pub const LAYOUT_HANDLE_TYPE: &str = LAYOUT_TYPE;
//RS 
//RS /// D-LAYOUT-CTOR1 (D-VERDICT-1306-1): `name :: Layout{ … }` — a D-DOTCTOR3
//RS /// typed-literal construction whose body is a comma-separated sequence of
//RS /// `Constraint` elements (same separators as `[T]{ … }`). Binds `name` (a
//RS /// `Layout`) in the enclosing scope (the handle outlives the literal, unlike
//RS /// `task.group`/`region`, since solved values are read after layout is
//RS /// defined). Each element must be a `>=`/`<=`/`==` comparison of layout
//RS /// values (a `Constraint`); the parser desugars bare `box.anchor` reads
//RS /// (`left`/`right`/`top`/`bottom`/`width`/`height`) into
//RS /// `name.h(box, anchor)` / `name.v(box, anchor)` calls, and `self.anchor`
//RS /// vivifies the container box named after the binding. Sema/codegen treat
//RS /// those exactly like any other `Layout` method call — no parallel checking
//RS /// mechanism; GATE 1/2 do all the real work.
//RS ///
//RS /// Retired `layout NAME { … }` keyword (D-LAYOUT1) is E2935 only.
//RS pub const FOREIGN_LAYOUT_KW: &str = "layout";
