//RS /// D-REACT1 (ratified 2026-06-22, option B): reactivity is an opt-in *library*,
//RS /// not core semantics. Ordinary binding semantics are unchanged; runtime
//RS /// reactivity ships as the `core.reactive` ring package. The surface is three
//RS /// explicit producers and their handle types — no new keyword or sigil (reactive
//RS /// values are ordinary values made with library calls, exactly as option B
//RS /// requires). `use core.reactive as reactive` exposes:
//RS ///   reactive.signal(initial) -> Signal<T>   — a mutable reactive source
//RS ///   reactive.derived(() -> expr) -> Derived<T> — a value recomputed from signals
//RS ///   reactive.computed(() -> expr)            — D-SIGNAL1 alias for `derived`
//RS ///   reactive.effect(() -> { … })             — a side effect re-run on change
//RS /// Methods: `Signal.get()/set(v)`, `Derived.get()`/`Computed.get()`. Dependency
//RS /// tracking is explicit-by-read (a `.get()` inside a derived/effect body subscribes).
//RS /// `#Reactive { … }` lowers to the effect job (D-REACTCORE1).
//RS pub const REACTIVE_MODULE: &str = "core.reactive";
//RS pub const TYPE_SIGNAL: &str = "Signal";
//RS pub const TYPE_DERIVED: &str = "Derived";
