//RS 
//RS /// D-INCR1 retired (owner decision 2026-09-28): `++` and `--` are not
//RS /// operators. The lexer keeps them only so the parser teaches E0160
//RS /// (`x += 1` / `x -= 1`) instead of reading `--x` as a double negation.
//RS pub const RETIRED_OP_PLUS_PLUS: &str = "++";
//RS pub const RETIRED_OP_MINUS_MINUS: &str = "--";
//RS 
//RS /// D-PATW (ratified 2026-06-19): `_` in a variant payload slot ignores that field and binds nothing.
//RS /// `_` remains a legal identifier character (digit-separator, S34) in all other positions.
//RS /// No bare `_` arm in a switch — only `else ->` acts as a catch-all.
//RS pub const PAT_WILDCARD_SLOT: &str = "_";
//RS 
//RS // D-PATR (ratified 2026-06-19): range patterns (`lo..hi`) reuse OP_RANGE (S22) at arm-head
//RS // level and inside variant payload slots. Open Int/Char subjects always still require `else`.
//RS 
//RS // D-PATO (ratified 2026-06-19), D-SHAPE-PIPE1=C (ratified 2026-07-15), and
//RS // D-BITOREXPR1=A (ratified 2026-08-28):
//RS // structural or-patterns and choice alternatives use OP_PIPE (single `|`).
//RS // `Active(id) | Reconnecting(id) -> …`; alternatives must bind the same names at the same types.
//RS // Value-position `|` is bitwise OR and binds above comparisons. No general bar
//RS // flow operator exists. `||` remains value-or / boolean-or; `|=` remains bitwise-or-assign under S17.
//RS 
//RS // D-ENUMDOT1 (ratified 2026-06-26, implemented): a leading `.` before a variant name in pattern
//RS // position (`.Circle(r)`, `.Empty`) is now accepted everywhere a variant pattern is written —
//RS // `if subject == { .Variant(b) -> … }`, `if x == .Variant(b)`, switch arms. The dot reads as
//RS // "a member of the inferred enum" and resolves S31's bare-name-vs-variable ambiguity without
//RS // requiring a qualified `Enum.Variant` spelling. Bare form still accepted; dot form is canonical
//RS // (the formatter always emits `.` before a Pattern::Variant name). No new keyword or sigil —
//RS // reuses OP_DOT (S21). Value-position dot (`.Red` where type is known) is D-ENUMDOT2 (open).
//RS 
//RS // D-TAG1 (ratified 2026-07-03): variant groups. A variant may enclose sub-variants
//RS // in `{ }` (`enum Damage { Physical { Blunt, Pierce } Fire { Burn, Scald } Cold }`), to any
//RS // depth. A group name matches its whole subtree in `==` pattern tests and dispatch arms
//RS // (`d == .Fire` is true for `.Fire.Burn`); exhaustiveness is checked at the group level;
//RS // payloads live on leaves only (E0331); a value is always a leaf — a group name is not a
//RS // value (E0332). Ships with the core counted multiset `Tally<T>` (`Tally.new()`, `add`,
//RS // `remove`, `has`, `count`; subtree queries stay an explicit `any` closure). No new keyword
//RS // or sigil — reuses `{ }` blocks, OP_DOT paths, and D-ENUMDOT1 leading-dot patterns.
//RS 
//RS // D-RANGE2 (c25, ratified): porting-hazard teaching errors for constructs Jet does NOT use.
//RS // E0318: `..=` (Rust inclusive range) — Jet's `..` is already inclusive; `0..=9` → teach `0..9`.
//RS // E0319: the retired loop `step` spelling in an arm head remains a porting hazard.
//RS 
